er, ServerEndpointConfig, and HandshakeRequest while leaving runtime behavior to a compatible implementation.\"\n- **`language`:** left absent, because this is a plain Java library and not language-specific.\n\nIf you allow edits, or tell me to apply the change another way, I'll make it.\nRan agent for jakarta.websocket:jakarta.websocket-api:2.3.0-M1 (exit 0). Log: /home/oracle/oracle/metadata2/graalvm-reachability-metadata/forge/local_repositories/forge_worktrees/9358-0d3679e0/build/agent-url-discovery-logs/jakarta.websocket-jakarta.websocket-api-2.3.0-M1.log\nCompleted populateArtifactURLs: invoked=1, prompted=0, skipped=0, overwriteExisting=false, verifyArtifactSources=false, limit=null\n\n[Incubating] Problems report is available at: file:///home/oracle/oracle/metadata2/graalvm-reachability-metadata/forge/local_repositories/forge_worktrees/9358-0d3679e0/build/reports/problems/problems-report.html\n\nDeprecated Gradle features were used in this build, making it incompatible with Gradle 10.\n\nYou can use '--warning-mode all' to show the individual deprecation warnings and determine if they come from your own scripts or plugins.\n\nFor more on this, please refer to https://docs.gradle.org/9.1.0/userguide/command_line_interface.html#sec:command_line_warnings in the Gradle documentation.\n\nBUILD SUCCESSFUL in 21s\n9 actionable tasks: 1 executed, 8 up-to-date\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1790876571930}}
