ou verified share the same mechanism. Include only versions you actually verified; when you cannot verify newer versions, record only 2.3.0-M1.\n31-\n32:On an unsupportable verdict, return instead:\n33-{\n34:  \"action\": \"skip_unsupported\",\n35:  \"summary\": \"one sentence naming the mechanism and why the image cannot perform it\",\n36-  \"skipped_versions\": [{\"version\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"mechanism sentence; later versions: '; unchanged from <first>'\"}, ...]\n37-}\n38:skipped_versions must include 2.3.0-M1; reasons are published verbatim in index.json and the pull request, so write them for a reader who has not seen this analysis. Never base the verdict on a red test, a library's own error type, or its error message — only on the mechanism you traced in the library's source. Any uncertainty at any step means repairable: attempting the fix is the safe default, a wrong skip freezes versions that were never attempted.\n39-\n40-Context (starting point):\n--\n44-    \"title\": \"[Automation] javac compile fails for jakarta.websocket:jakarta.websocket-api:2.3.0-M1\",\n45-    \"label\": \"fails-javac-compile\",\n46:    \"body\": \"## javac compile on ubuntu-latest / JDK 25 / mode current-defaults\\n\\nFailure kind: javac compile\\nOS: ubuntu-latest\\nJDK: 25\\nNative-image mode: current-defaults\\nReproducer: `env GVM_TCK_LV=2.3.0-M1 GVM_TCK_NATIVE_IMAGE_MODE=current-defaults ./gradlew clean compileTestJava -Pcoordinates=jakarta.websocket:jakarta.websocket-api:2.1.0`\\nRunner log: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/actions/runs/32316088693\\nLast 300 lines of the log:\\n```console\\n========================================================================================\\n run-consecutive-tests input\\n========================================================================================\\nCoordinates: jakarta.websocket:jakarta.websocket-api:2.1.0\\nRaw versions JSON: [\\n  \\\"2.3.0-M1\\\",\\n  \\\"2.3.0-M2\\\"\\n]\\nParsed version coun