ikely failing stage is dependency resolution before Java or native-image compilation. Repeated Gradle runs could not parse the `2.3.0-M1` POM because its `jakarta.websocket-all:2.3.0-M1` parent chain references unavailable `org.eclipse.ee4j:project:2.0.0-SNAPSHOT`. All six iterations failed to resolve this; one attempted workaround also caused a Gradle DSL error (`Could not find method withModule()`). Metrics report failure, 6 iterations, 0 generated LOC, no metadata, and identical starting/ending commits, so no verified repair was produced.\n\nInspect:\n- `human-intervention-logs/jakarta.websocket:jakarta.websocket-api:2.3.0-M1/gradle-test/gradle-test-2026-10-01T17-40-30-921599Z.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/jakarta.websocket:jakarta.websocket-api:2.3.0-M1/gradle-test/gradle-test-2026-10-01T17-39-45-132252Z.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/jakarta.websocket:jakarta.websocket-api:2.3.0-M1/fix-javac-fail/pi-generation-2026-10-01T17-35-02-898261Z.log`\n- `stats/jakarta.websocket/jakarta.websocket-api/2.3.0-M1/execution-metrics.json`\n\nManual next steps:\n1. Confirm whether `2.3.0-M1` can be resolved reproducibly from supported repositories, and compare its POM with `2.3.0-M2`.\n2. If support is required, add a repository-approved dependency-resolution workaround and rerun `compileTestJava` and `test` for this coordinate.\n3. If the published milestone is irreparably unresolvable, record the appropriate skipped-version disposition instead of treating this as a test-source or Native Image failure.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_04a05bb5f71f3c2e016abe9bb2714487d29df0ffe1f052b6c0\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 33176, "output": 1027, "cacheRead": 92032, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 516, "totalTokens": 126235, "cost": {"input": 0.132704, "output": 0.020540000000000003, "cacheRead": 0.03681280000000001, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.1900568}}, "stopReason"